From 342d8a97226b17d52b082843644147d0a0513d98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:24:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin I-442: MSAA on Vulkan from gxMultisample - the world
 and the character create/select scene render multisampled

- Sample count: the format's gxMultisample, clamped to the device's colour/depth/sampled-depth counts; needs the own
  back buffer and a sampled depth-only format; 1 = the old path untouched. Logged once (Vulkan.log "MSAA: ... used").
- msaaColour/msaaDepth beside the 1x back images; an N-sample pass class inside the MSAA window (the world scene, and
  the glue model scene via the new g_gxModelScene seam around CSimpleModelFFX::Render); samples in the pass-class key,
  PassInfo/pipelines, the persisted pipeline keys (kKeysVersion 3) and WXL_VkRenderContext.samples.
- Coherence: resolve on read (BackBuffer: vkCmdResolveImage; SceneDepth: sample-0 fullscreen depth resolve), re-seed the
  MSAA images from the 1x ones after a stage writes the frame; WXL_VK_STAGE_READS_COLOR (CataSceneCapture) skips CopyOut.
- MSAA takes priority (user): with MSAA on, no G-buffer; hdSunShadows stays off and hdAO uses depth normals, their Info
  lines say so.
- Occlusion queries divided by the pass's sample count (sun glare).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJVC4feQ4s15e9bNRoN
